		{
			"id": "112355117990297166",
			"parentId": "112354996636921648",
			"url": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat/112355117990297166",
			"author": {
				"name": "Zach Leatherman",
				"url": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/accounts/avatars/109/286/461/031/266/152/original/dc489c3746a44e00.png"
			},
			"date": "2024-04-29T15:04:05.508Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://front-end.social/@robinwhittleton\" class=\"u-url mention\">@<span>robinwhittleton</span></a></span> yeah, it depends on the font and the use case but usually saves KB when you compare two font files of the same typeface versus one variable! also solves the independent repaint/reflow problem: <a href=\"https://www.zachleat.com/web/fout-vs-foit/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" translate=\"no\"><span class=\"invisible\">https://www.</span><span class=\"\">zachleat.com/web/fout-vs-foit/</span><span class=\"invisible\"></span></a></p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "112355148037963488",
			"parentId": "112355117990297166",
			"url": "https://front-end.social/@robinwhittleton/112355148020694672",
			"author": {
				"name": "Robin Whittleton",
				"url": "https://front-end.social/@robinwhittleton",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/111/368/535/474/087/976/original/bbcae0cbe7e6c684.jpg"
			},
			"date": "2024-04-29T15:11:43.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> maybe we’ve heavily optimised our files already, but I was seeing more KB with a variable font. Partially this was down to an unknown-to-me semibold in Noto Sans variable. But even after stripping that out, the axes added enough that it wasn’t worth it.</p><p>Where we did see a big benefit from variable fonts was (ironically) not in the font itself, but in halving the size of the CJK font chunk CSS.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
